          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "les coulisses — \"wings, backstage\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Avant le spectacle, les acteurs attendent dans les coulisses. Before the show the actors wait in the wings."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Mostly plural. Dans les coulisses — behind the scenes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "les coulisses comes from coulisse \"a groove that something slides in\", built on couler \"to flow, to slide\", from Latin cōlāre \"to strain\" (Lewis & Short): the sets slid in grooves at the side of the stage."
            }
          ]
        },
